<title>USA: Moody's applauds US judge ruling in Colo case.</title>
<headline>Moody's applauds US judge ruling in Colo case.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Tuesday it is &quot;gratified&quot; by a U.S. judge's dismissal of federal antitrust and related state law claims filed against the company by Colorado's largest school district.</p>
<p>&quot;Moody's applauds this decision, and its wider implications for the efficient functioning of the global capital markets,&quot; the firm, a unit of Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp., said following U.S. District Judge William Downes' dismissal of all five charges filed by Jefferson County School District against the company over the adequacy of a 1993 unsolicited rating.</p>
</text>
